then the the planning commission serves as a recommending body to the governing body who implements the plan through ordinances and such like the unified development code Uh the plan the comprehensive plan is available on our website Again it's multiple uh pieces of the comprehensive plan and it's our parks and recck master plan our transportation master plan and the community plan Uh we presently have funding to update the community plan and we're trying to get that RFP or RF RFP out the door but things keep our other projects keep on getting getting brought up that we're working on Again the unified development code is what we see the most often here Um it's the processes that are defined to go from point A to point B in the development world Some are administrative where they just go to staff and

they're done Others do require that they go in front of the board of adjustment for approval or they go to the governing body for approval after review and recommendation by you all the planning commission We talked about the annual review requirement today Um that does happen on the second meeting of every February which falls on a Tuesday after the president's day weekend Again the boards that you all are most familiar with are the planning commission which is you all guide growth master plan primarily recommendations the governing body uh the board of adjustment This is one that has some decision-making authority uh acting chair led uh did serve on that for quite some time Um they hear appeals of um

administrative decisions They also more a final decision maker on variances and conditional use uh approvals such as uh apartments complexes in certain zone districts There are a variety of other um commissions and boards and committees that the the department does um have a connection with including specialty committees like ATAC the active transportation advisory committee which I was meeting with prior to this meeting which they're probably still meeting upstairs as well or they just got out No one showed up I told them they could share their ideas if they wanted to Um here's just a snapshot of what you all do which you all are uh pretty accustomed to knowing and we will try to share with you anything new that pops up Uh

things that are new are urban renewal plans and projects recently and DDA development projects Those are ones that you don't see as often but they do uh make an appearance in front of you all Public hearing process This is pretty straightforward The applicant makes a presentation Then staff makes a presentation the staff report The planning commission can uh ask questions of staff for the applicant Then there's public testimony a public hearing This is the official public hearing in all of our our uh zoning action items except for annexations Those are in front of the governing body and those happen at introduction of the annexation ordinance Um technically once the public hearing is called closed um

then you all can move into deliberation talk about how you want to vote You can ask staff for further uh clarification if you wish Um it's strongly advised that you don't reopen the public hearing as a chair to take on more comment um just because that gets to be a little bit bit squirly It leads to people easily being able to lose control of the meeting And with that in mind you know if you do start asking staff a lot of questions sometimes the uh the audience might feel that they should have the ability to chime in So if you do have uh questions on how motion should be formed please do it But if it's just general questions try to do that um

