we would like to be excused when it comes time for that Okay that also Uh oh here that is correct Yes that would be the appropriate time That would be the appropriate time to identify if you have a conflict of interest which I'll just jump to that really quick So a conflict of interest is a situation in which an individual has competing interests or loyalties Let's use uh Commissioner Olsen for example Um let's say he's starting a bicycle shop in town and he needs to reszone a property in the middle of his neighborhood to community business or even light industrial because he just wants different building standards so he can operate his business It would not be appropriate for Lonnie to take a a vote on that item because he has a demonstrated conflict of interest because there's conflicting loyalties there for him it would be best that he would leave the room um

and then have someone else present that project on his behalf Same thing is if um you all had a sister or a brother or a mother or a son and they were asking for um a specific recommendation for approval you want to avoid avoid that because there's a perception of favoritism there And also if you are partners in a real estate group um and you have a potential financial gain because of this action that would be a concern as well Those would be conflicts that you would note and then you would be excused from voting on those items We haven't had too many conflicts um on this board but uh we have on a couple of others where they've um

abstained from voting and recuse themselves But we do ask that they do leave the room you know during that vote because even your presence your mannerisms just your just being there it could have um an effect on the board Commissions boards and committees aren't the best at leaving the room Sometimes they sit there and I'm like "A weren't you listening during training?" So um open meetings act This is something that is very important Um this doesn't mean that you know six of you are hanging out at a holiday party You know you happen to run in a holiday party together It's when you're starting to conduct public business So you all could all be hanging out at some different event because you're volunteering for planning month in October You know you're serving chicken wings for everybody or something like that you know you could all

be together but the moment you're like "Oh let's talk about this new apartment complex that's proposed and you start to have something that would resemble what would be discussed here that's where the issue is issue is Um so if you have a quorum of people a quorum of board members they're talking about a board topic you have an issue But if you have a less than quorum and say you're studying something like block length amendments you have less than a majority you know you could have a subcommittee that could talk freely and private there and then you would report back to the whole planning commission what your findings are So I've uh kind of reduced um

my take on this I always operate under extreme caution and said avoid a quorum being present at all times But now I've loosened it to just say just don't talk business if you're having more of a quorum um present Now this includes things like Facebook posts uh text message strings email correspondence Um try not to hit reply all and definitely don't start talking about um an upcoming agenda item on any of those those items This is another good one I haven't seen this motion yet I think it'd be funny if I did All those in favor of what we discussed in our email thread at Larry's son's birthday party say "I I I have no idea what's going on I thought this meeting was open." So

